<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Danish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Denmark is a Scandinavian kingdom that, as Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s principal rival for control of the Baltic in the early modern period. Swedish victories over Denmark, culminating in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> (1658), were central to the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>, while Danish attacks after the Swedish defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709 contributed to its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/denmark.jpg" alt="Denmark" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Madden and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Denmark.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
